# Working with Files

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `touch notes.txt` | Create an empty file or update its timestamp |
| `mkdir projects` | Create a directory |
| `cp source.txt copy.txt` | Copy a file |
| `mv old.txt new.txt` | Move or rename a file |
| `cat notes.txt` | Print a file's contents |
| `less notes.txt` | Read a file one screen at a time |
| `head -n 10 notes.txt` | Print the first 10 lines |
| `tail -n 10 notes.txt` | Print the last 10 lines |
| `grep "text" notes.txt` | Find matching text in a file |
| `find . -name "*.txt"` | Find matching files below the current directory |

Be careful with commands that delete or overwrite data. In particular,
`rm` normally deletes files without moving them to a recycle bin. Check paths
and arguments before running it.
